  "summary": "Recent MD studies benchmark bilayer analysis software and system size while an unsupervised method now classifies coexisting lipid phases.",
  "synthesis": "Across these items, the common thread is methodology for extracting structural and phase information from molecular dynamics trajectories of lipid membranes and confined liquids. A preprint examines how POPC bilayer size (256 to 1024 lipids) and hydration affect lipid membrane analysis, benchmarking CPPTRAJ, GROMACS, MDAnalysis, and LiPyphilic. A published study introduces an unsupervised approach that pixelates lipid packing density and applies a two-component threshold to classify coexisting lipid phases in bilayer simulations. DynoPore, a published Python package, addresses structure, mobility, and lifetimes for liquids confined in pores. The new element is the unsupervised phase-recognition route, set alongside systematic assessment of system size and software dependence.",
